---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PostList from '../components/PostList.astro';
import { SITE, SOCIALS } from '../consts';
import { publish } from '../utils/format';

const writing = publish(await getCollection('writing')).slice(0, 5);
---

<Base isHome>
    <article>
        <h1>Jenish Kothari</h1>

        <p>
            <img
                src="/images/jenish.webp"
                alt="Jenish Kothari"
                width="60"
                height="60"
                loading="lazy"
            />
            I'm Jenish. Software Engineer II at <strong>Adobe</strong>, MS CS from
            Northeastern. I post-train small open models to do work that usually
            needs frontier models &mdash; in production, and in the open.
        </p>

        <p>
            Post-training is the day job and the hobby: SFT, reasoning
            distillation, DPO, and GRPO. At Adobe I distilled a production LLM
            down to a <strong>3B parameter model, cutting inference cost 10&times;
            while holding 72% of GPT-4 benchmarks</strong>. On my own time I do
            the same thing for text-to-SQL, evaluated by executing every
            generated query against the real database and comparing result sets
            &mdash; no fuzzy string matching, no exact-match SQL scoring.
        </p>

        <p>
            The thread running through all of it is <em>local</em>. A 7B that fits
            on one GPU and matches a 1.6T frontier model is worth more to most
            teams than an API call, so that's what I optimize for.
        </p>

        <p>
            <strong>Start here: <a href="/start-here/">Start Here</a></strong>
        </p>

        <h3>Latest writing</h3>
        <PostList items={writing} showDescription />
        <p><a href="/writing/">All writing &rarr;</a></p>

        <h3>Elsewhere</h3>
        <p>
            Models and datasets on <a href={SOCIALS.huggingface}>Hugging Face</a>,
            code on <a href={SOCIALS.github}>GitHub</a>, and short-form thinking on
            <a href={SOCIALS.x}>X</a>. Also on
            <a href={SOCIALS.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a> and
            <a href={SOCIALS.kaggle}>Kaggle</a>.
        </p>
        <p>Email: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a></p>
    </article>
</Base>
